            <ArticleTitle>NNMT: A Bad Actor in Fat Makes Good in Liver.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>200-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2015.07.017</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(15)00346-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High adipose expression of NNMT, an enzyme that converts nicotinamide to 1-methyl-nicotinamide, correlates with adiposity. Though murine NNMT knockdown in fat and liver prevents weight gain on high-fat diet, Hong et al. (2015) now show that high hepatic expression of NNMT improves lipid parameters via SIRT1 stabilization.</AbstractText>
